      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:3:22:6",
      "text": [
        " تَنَوَّقُوا فِي الْأَكْفَانِ فَإِنَّكُمْ تُبْعَثُونَ بِهَا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad Bin Isa, from Muhammad Bin Al Husayn, from Abdul Rahman Bin Abu Hashim, from Abu Khadeeja, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Be choosy regarding the shrouds for you would be Resurrected in it’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "6. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Isa from Muhammad ibn al-Husayn from ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn abu Hashim from abu Khadijah who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘Try to make your shrouds look beautiful; you will be raised with your shrouds.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
